      "date": "2026-11-10 21:39:21.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 2: Code-Review+1\n\nThe fix looks right for the test_33 case. I checked that \"lfsck_stop -M\" returns 0 when no LFSCK is running on ost1, so step (7) does not fail when the resumed LFSCK has already finished. The \"!= paused\" wait also passes when it is already \"completed\".\n\nOne question: the LU-21029 description reports test_38 on ldiskfs, not test_33. Tests 33 to 37 each run a full layout LFSCK, so I think an LFSCK left over from test_32a cannot still be running in test_38. If that is right, test_38 may need a separate look, and the ticket could stay open after this lands. Is that how you see it?",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 2
    },
